1
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:18,840
♪ I notice every glance ♪

2
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:23,680
♪ The way you look at me ♪

3
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:29,120
♪ And what they're hiding inside ♪

4
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:32,960
♪ I think we might be the same ♪

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,200
♪ Hiding our true feelings ♪

6
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,000
♪ Not wanting them to come out ♪

7
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,680
♪ But the closer we get ♪

8
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:47,520
♪ The more my heart wavers ♪

9
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:52,120
♪ I want to surrender to every voice in my heart ♪

10
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:54,520
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

11
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:58,000
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

12
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,560
I’m sorry, Ms. Kasira.

13
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,840
I thought I had met someone familiar.

14
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:04,599
Uttawadee,

15
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:05,840
this is only the beginning.

16
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,000
If you hate me this much,

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,039
why keep me here

18
00:01:13,039 --> 00:01:14,160
as your eyesore?

19
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:16,720
A hired hand has no right to ask me that.

20
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,480
Oh!

21
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:21,920
Oh!

22
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:24,640
Oh!

23
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,240
Oh! What's wrong?

24
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,240
Oh!

25
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:29,400
Oh!

26
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,640
You're burning up.

27
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:37,400
Oh.

28
00:01:37,479 --> 00:01:39,320
You're so forgetful, Doctor.

29
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:41,920
Oh!

30
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,440
What's wrong with Oh?

31
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,400
Ms. Song, what happened?

32
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,000
I don't know.

33
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,640
We were just talking and Oh fainted.

34
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:53,640
Oh, can you hear me? Oh.

35
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,160
Oh?

36
00:01:55,759 --> 00:01:56,840
Oh.

37
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,360
Oh.

38
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,320
It's probably a fever.

39
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,600
Which room is hers? I'll carry her there.

40
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:20,160
No need.

41
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,400
Ms. Song,

42
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:24,840
I'm a doctor.

43
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,600
Please hand Oh over to me.

44
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:42,680
This way, please.

45
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,680
Yes.

46
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,520
Her fever is very high.

47
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:56,680
Has Oh been getting too little sleep lately?

48
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,360
Not as far as I can tell.

49
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:02,440
But when Oh came back in just now,

50
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:03,680
she was drenched in sweat.

51
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:05,240
She said she walked in

52
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,400
from entrance of the alley.

53
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:07,480
Could that be related?

54
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,480
Walked in?

55
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,000
So it's a fever. Then what?

56
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:20,840
What medicine does she need,

57
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:21,880
and how do we give it?

58
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:27,480
Once she's come around

59
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,520
and isn't nauseous,

60
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,000
give her small sips of water

61
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,000
or electrolyte solution.

62
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,880
For now, sponge her down to

63
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,400
bring her temperature down first.

64
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:35,960
Then I'll go downstairs

65
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,840
and get what we need for the sponge bath.

66
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,079
Will you do it yourself, Doctor?

67
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,360
Well...

68
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,160
No.

69
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,240
Oh.

70
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,920
Then I'll do it myself.

71
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,120
No need.

72
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:57,000
I'll do it myself.

73
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:00,200
Go down and get the things.

74
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,320
Yes, ma'am.

75
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:07,960
Oh is normally a healthy person

76
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,840
who doesn't get sick easily,

77
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,320
and she's always taken

78
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,360
good care of herself.

79
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,080
Or maybe...

80
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,720
Oh isn't suited to working here?

81
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:21,040
Are you saying we work people too hard?

82
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:22,680
That's not what I mean.

83
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,520
I just feel terrible that I'm the one

84
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,200
who made Oh have to go through this.

85
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,120
Like this?

86
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,320
Like what, exactly?

87
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,520
You're overthinking it.

88
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,240
She just fainted.

89
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,680
Cloth and water are here.

90
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:45,360
I think I should take Oh to the hospital,

91
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:48,400
so we don't have to trouble anyone here.

92
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,520
No need.

93
00:04:50,159 --> 00:04:52,080
I'll take care of my own people myself.

94
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,720
Uttawadee is an employee here.

95
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,720
We have a welfare policy that looks

96
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:01,360
after every employee when they're ill.

97
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,600
If she isn't better by tomorrow,

98
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,240
I'll take her to the hospital myself.

99
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,120
Cream, see doc out,

100
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,160
then go look after Mother,

101
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,760
in case Nueng needs anything.

102
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:14,920
Yes, ma'am.

103
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:23,760
Goodbye, Doctor.

104
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:24,640
Goodbye.

105
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,640
Employee welfare?

106
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,920
When I got sick,

107
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,280
I never got anything like that.

108
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,600
Then again,

109
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:42,200
I did once get to stay in the hospital.

110
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:44,560
I guess that counts.

111
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:49,560
♪ I want to tell you so you'll understand ♪

112
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:53,960
♪ But how much longer ♪

113
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:58,680
♪ Can I keep all these words inside? ♪

114
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:03,600
♪ Every time we meet ♪

115
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:07,360
♪ How can I keep pretending
When deep down inside ♪

116
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:10,720
♪ I just want to say it out loud? ♪

117
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:14,120
♪ But the closer we get ♪

118
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:18,360
♪ The more my heart wavers ♪

119
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:22,480
♪ I want to surrender to every voice in my heart ♪

120
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:25,000
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

121
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,280
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

122
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:33,640
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

123
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:37,080
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

124
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:41,360
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

125
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:49,440
♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪

126
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:58,560
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪

127
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,200
Hey.

128
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,120
What are you thinking?

129
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:42,960
I'm not in the mood for anything

130
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:43,960
with a sick person.

131
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,280
Who changed my clothes?

132
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,320
Was it you?

133
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,080
What of it?

134
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,720
Embarrassed?

135
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,080
What is there for me

136
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,200
to get excited about you?

137
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,560
Nothing.

138
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,080
What's there to be embarrassed about?

139
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:08,240
Thank you for taking care of me,

140
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,200
but I don't need it right now.

141
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:18,080
Please leave my room.

142
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:23,240
I'll leave, for sure.

143
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,760
I never wanted to come into your life.

144
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:15,400
(Medicine time for Oh)

145
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,160
The fever's come back up.

146
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:52,800
Please just leave.

147
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,400
I don't have the strength

148
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,400
to argue with you.

149
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:58,800
Time to take your medicine.

150
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,360
I can take it myself.

151
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,280
You don't need to.

152
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:18,040
Take the medicine, and then I'll go.

153
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:55,400
♪ I notice every glance ♪

154
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:59,840
♪ The way you look at me ♪

155
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:05,280
♪ And what they're hiding inside ♪

156
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:09,400
♪ I think we might be the same ♪

157
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:13,360
♪ Hiding our true feelings ♪

158
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:16,560
♪ Not wanting them to come out ♪

159
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:19,880
♪ But the closer we get ♪

160
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:23,800
♪ The more my heart wavers ♪

161
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:28,480
♪ I want to surrender to every voice in my heart ♪

162
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:30,920
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

163
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:34,440
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

164
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:39,720
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

165
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:43,000
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

166
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:47,280
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

167
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:55,440
♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪

168
00:13:55,480 --> 00:14:02,000
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪

169
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,320
Don't go thinking that what I did

170
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:55,960
last night was because I was worried.

171
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,880
I just don't want anyone dying in my house.

172
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:06,880
And judging by the state of you...

173
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:08,680
take the day off today.

174
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:10,640
I don't want anyone spreading germs

175
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:11,600
around the house.

176
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:44,800
Ms. Song.

177
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:18,680
Cream.

178
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,320
Mm?

179
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:20,520
What are you staring at?

180
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:21,640
Is something wrong?

181
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:24,080
It's Ms. Song.

182
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,800
She went into her room last night

183
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:27,000
and hasn't come out at all.

184
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,480
She didn't eat,

185
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,480
and she didn't go to work today either.

186
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:34,320
If you want to know,

187
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,040
go knock on her door.

188
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:38,000
Gosh, no way.

189
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,760
No, thanks. Not worth the risk.

190
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:43,280
But if something's happened to her,

191
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:44,840
no one will know.

192
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:48,120
Well...

193
00:17:11,119 --> 00:17:12,160
Ms. Kasira.

194
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:17,720
Ms. Kasira.

195
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:35,240
May I come in?

196
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:55,680
Ms. Kasira.

197
00:17:58,360 --> 00:17:59,360
Ms. Kasira.

198
00:19:56,240 --> 00:19:57,320
Why did you come in?

199
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,640
Do you realize you're unwell?

200
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,280
It's just a headache.

201
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:04,560
A headache,

202
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,480
a fever.

203
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,040
You're unwell.

204
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:13,440
If I'm sick, it's because

205
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,560
I caught it from you.

206
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:16,280
You're a walking germ.

207
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:20,360
Then I'll go find some medicine for you,

208
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,600
so your germs can clear up.

209
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,120
Don't bother.

210
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:26,600
If you have this much energy,

211
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,440
get up and wash your face.

212
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,600
Then you can eat and take your medicine.

213
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:33,160
You're really...

214
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:34,280
Get up, please.

215
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:02,320
Are you all right?

216
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:29,480
Yes, Ms. Nueng.

217
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:31,600
Cream, how is Mother?

218
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,400
The madam is asleep.

219
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:36,360
And Ms. Oh?

220
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,200
She was unwell. She's better now, right?

221
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:39,840
Yes, she's better.

222
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:42,320
Oh isn't the one to worry about.

223
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,080
The one to worry about

224
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:45,480
is Ms. Song.

225
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:47,640
Why?

226
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,560
She's been shut up in her room

227
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:50,640
since last night.

228
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:53,560
Oh is in there checking on her right now.

229
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,280
Oh went in to check on her?

230
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:57,160
Yes.

231
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,040
Well...

232
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,320
Um...

233
00:22:03,040 --> 00:22:04,040
Then I'll come over.

234
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:05,480
That's all for now.

235
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:45,960
One more bite, please.

236
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:02,480
Just one more.

237
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:17,600
Your medicine.

238
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:49,000
Wait until it's fully dissolved

239
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:49,920
before you drink it.

240
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:50,960
Once you've finished,

241
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:52,480
lie down and rest so you'll get better.

242
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:04,360
Because of you, I turned out like this.

243
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:07,680
Aren't you going to

244
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:08,840
take some responsibility?

245
00:24:30,680 --> 00:24:31,680
Fine.

246
00:24:32,080 --> 00:24:33,360
I'll take responsibility myself.

247
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:31,960
I've taken responsibility now.

248
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:46,120
Oh, there you are.

249
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:48,680
I've been looking all over for you.

250
00:27:52,040 --> 00:27:53,080
Nueng,

251
00:27:54,560 --> 00:27:55,680
if you were coming over,

252
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:57,120
why didn't you call and tell me?

253
00:28:05,240 --> 00:28:06,920
I heard you weren't well.

254
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:09,240
Mm, I'm better now.

255
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:21,840
Is something the matter, Nueng?

256
00:28:23,480 --> 00:28:24,480
I should be asking you.

257
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:26,200
Is there something you want to tell me?

258
00:28:29,520 --> 00:28:30,520
No, nothing.

259
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:37,000
You're not going to admit it?

260
00:28:37,360 --> 00:28:38,640
About the new nurse.

261
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:48,600
Well...

262
00:28:49,360 --> 00:28:50,480
There's nothing to admit.

263
00:28:52,360 --> 00:28:53,480
She works well.

264
00:28:54,080 --> 00:28:55,080
She's fine.

265
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:02,280
It's only the us left, you know.

266
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:04,360
If you won't tell me,

267
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:06,600
there's nothing I can do.

268
00:29:07,280 --> 00:29:08,360
I'll go home, then.

269
00:29:09,040 --> 00:29:10,160
Wait, Nueng.

270
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:11,520
It's not like that.

271
00:29:17,320 --> 00:29:19,320
Tell me what you want to know.

272
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:22,080
If you say there's nothing,

273
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:23,200
what is there for me to

274
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:24,240
be suspicious about?

275
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:30,400
Okay.

276
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:32,520
You see...

277
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,200
Would you mind, Nueng,

278
00:29:39,200 --> 00:29:40,200
if...

279
00:29:41,200 --> 00:29:42,720
I told you that...

280
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:49,360
I like women?

281
00:29:53,720 --> 00:29:55,560
That's all I wanted to hear, Song.

282
00:29:59,280 --> 00:30:00,280
Song,

283
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:03,120
whoever you like is your right.

284
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:06,080
And whoever my little sister likes,

285
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:07,280
whatever kind of person,

286
00:30:07,320 --> 00:30:08,520
this big sister welcomes it.

287
00:30:10,640 --> 00:30:11,840
The thing is,

288
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:13,640
this nurse is my ex.

289
00:30:15,160 --> 00:30:17,160
We dated back in university...

290
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:28,880
So that's how it went.

291
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:34,760
But she seems so sweet,

292
00:30:34,760 --> 00:30:36,600
and she seems like a really good person.

293
00:30:37,360 --> 00:30:38,640
I can hardly believe she'd be

294
00:30:38,640 --> 00:30:39,920
the kind of person who did that.

295
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:41,360
What would you know, Nueng?

296
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:43,360
You've only met her a few times.

297
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:45,520
Well, I can see she looks after Mother

298
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:46,720
with more dedication than

299
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:47,760
anyone before her.

300
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,400
You have to admit it,

301
00:30:49,720 --> 00:30:52,000
Mother's condition has visibly improved.

302
00:30:53,040 --> 00:30:54,840
She recognizes us faster than she used to.

303
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:59,880
If she weren't truly committed and caring,

304
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:01,320
I don't think Mother would have

305
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:02,520
improved this much.

306
00:31:03,360 --> 00:31:04,800
If our family didn't have money,

307
00:31:05,560 --> 00:31:06,800
she wouldn't be sitting here

308
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:07,840
doing this for us.

309
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:11,440
And don't you think

310
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:14,480
there might be more reasons than that?

311
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:17,000
I'd like to think so, Nueng,

312
00:31:18,360 --> 00:31:19,720
but there's nothing that lets me

313
00:31:19,760 --> 00:31:20,920
think of it any other way.

314
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:23,040
Then if that's how you see her,

315
00:31:23,640 --> 00:31:25,080
why do you still keep her on?

316
00:31:38,320 --> 00:31:40,080
You must have your reasons.

317
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:44,000
But if you ever want to tell me,

318
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:46,280
I'm always ready to listen.

319
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:24,320
Ms. Song,

320
00:32:24,360 --> 00:32:27,200
here's the medicine Oh sorted out for you.

321
00:32:31,200 --> 00:32:32,360
Morning,

322
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:34,440
(Morning)(Noon)
noon,

323
00:32:34,480 --> 00:32:35,480
(Morning)(Noon)(Evening)
and evening.

324
00:32:37,040 --> 00:32:38,440
Where's the person who sorted it?

325
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:40,000
Why didn't she come tell me herself?

326
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:42,160
Today's Oh's day off.

327
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:44,040
She finished sorting your medicine and

328
00:32:44,080 --> 00:32:45,240
went out first thing this morning.

329
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:01,680
(Morning)

330
00:33:10,520 --> 00:33:11,960
Last night Mom complained that

331
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:13,880
her body ached so much she couldn't sleep.

332
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:15,160
She only just fell asleep

333
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,440
not long before you got here.

334
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:19,240
Oh.

335
00:33:19,280 --> 00:33:20,520
I think the painkillers

336
00:33:20,520 --> 00:33:22,320
are starting to stop working.

337
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:27,280
I'll call Professor Smith and ask him.

338
00:33:35,040 --> 00:33:36,120
Hello, Professor.

339
00:33:36,600 --> 00:33:38,600
I wanted to consult you about something.

340
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:40,880
Ong says Mom's body aches

341
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,560
have gotten worse lately.

342
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:44,960
The medicine she was given doesn't seem to

343
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:46,280
control the symptoms anymore,

344
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:47,480
and she's eating less too.

345
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:49,720
Then could Ong bring your mother

346
00:33:49,760 --> 00:33:50,880
to the hospital tomorrow?

347
00:33:50,920 --> 00:33:51,960
I'll have a colleague

348
00:33:51,960 --> 00:33:53,000
take the consultation.

349
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:54,920
Of course.

350
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:56,200
Thank you so much, Professor.

351
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:58,000
Don't mention it.

352
00:33:58,040 --> 00:33:59,040
It's nothing.

353
00:33:59,880 --> 00:34:01,320
Where are you right now?

354
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:02,880
I'm at my mother's place.

355
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:04,600
I'll be heading back to

356
00:34:04,600 --> 00:34:06,080
the other house in a little while.

357
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:08,000
Then I'll swing by and pick you up.

358
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:10,000
There's no need.

359
00:34:10,239 --> 00:34:11,480
I can get back on my own.

360
00:34:11,679 --> 00:34:12,880
I don't want to trouble you.

361
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:14,960
Don't worry about it.

362
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:18,080
I have to stop by somewhere

363
00:34:18,120 --> 00:34:19,120
in that area anyway.

364
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:20,440
See you then.

365
00:34:21,880 --> 00:34:22,840
All right.

366
00:34:22,880 --> 00:34:24,080
Thank you, professor.

367
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:05,800
(Nurse Oh)

368
00:35:14,880 --> 00:35:16,120
When is she coming back?

369
00:35:18,120 --> 00:35:19,480
Oh,

370
00:35:20,080 --> 00:35:21,280
your clothes.

371
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:24,400
Ong,

372
00:35:25,800 --> 00:35:26,800
that's too much.

373
00:35:26,840 --> 00:35:28,640
I haven't worn everything from last time.

374
00:35:28,640 --> 00:35:29,840
Just look at this first.

375
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:32,600
Take it, Oh, it suits you.

376
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:34,800
I want to see you dressed up nicely.

377
00:35:37,840 --> 00:35:39,600
Tomorrow, once the doctor's visit is done,

378
00:35:39,640 --> 00:35:41,040
update me on Mom's condition.

379
00:35:41,080 --> 00:35:42,240
Will do. Message received.

380
00:35:43,080 --> 00:35:44,400
You're the sweetest.

381
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:48,960
Take care of yourself.

382
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:50,400
See you soon.

383
00:35:50,600 --> 00:35:52,120
Of course. You too.

384
00:35:53,200 --> 00:35:54,240
Come here, a hug.

385
00:35:59,560 --> 00:36:01,160
I'm definitely going to miss you.

386
00:36:01,320 --> 00:36:03,040
I'll come back to visit again next week.

387
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:04,240
Mm.

388
00:36:04,480 --> 00:36:05,480
Call me.

389
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:07,320
Okay.

390
00:36:07,360 --> 00:36:08,400
Call, call, call.

391
00:36:08,440 --> 00:36:09,440
Okay.

392
00:36:54,320 --> 00:36:55,440
Flirting with everyone.

393
00:36:57,560 --> 00:36:58,560
Cream!

394
00:36:58,680 --> 00:36:59,720
Um,

395
00:37:00,120 --> 00:37:01,200
yes, Ms. Song?

396
00:37:01,440 --> 00:37:03,280
Tell the nurse to come see me in my office!

397
00:37:03,880 --> 00:37:04,960
But Oh is still...

398
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:08,320
Yes, ma'am.

399
00:37:14,040 --> 00:37:15,200
You had me called in here.

400
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:16,440
What is it, Ms. Kasira?

401
00:37:19,720 --> 00:37:20,800
Impressive.

402
00:37:21,120 --> 00:37:22,720
Last night you slept with one person,

403
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:24,320
and today you go off with another.

404
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:26,560
So, did you get your fill?

405
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:30,680
If believing that puts your mind at ease,

406
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:32,160
then believe whatever you like.

407
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:34,640
You're not even going to defend yourself?

408
00:37:34,760 --> 00:37:35,920
What if I told you

409
00:37:36,080 --> 00:37:37,680
I went home to see my mother,

410
00:37:38,200 --> 00:37:39,960
and the professor had a business nearby,

411
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:41,400
so he picked me up at the house

412
00:37:41,440 --> 00:37:42,720
and dropped me off here?

413
00:37:42,920 --> 00:37:44,040
And those bags are things

414
00:37:44,080 --> 00:37:45,320
my sister sent with me.

415
00:37:45,360 --> 00:37:46,440
Would you believe me?

416
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:48,360
What a coincidence.

417
00:37:49,440 --> 00:37:51,080
You coincidentally visit your mother,

418
00:37:51,200 --> 00:37:52,360
he coincidentally stops by,

419
00:37:53,160 --> 00:37:55,080
and someone delivers you right to the door.

420
00:37:55,200 --> 00:37:57,200
Yes. That's really how it was.

421
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:58,800
And I'm supposed to believe you?

422
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:00,200
Why wouldn't you believe me?

423
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:02,120
Because you've lied to me before!

424
00:38:04,120 --> 00:38:05,760
I used to believe everything you said,

425
00:38:06,680 --> 00:38:07,840
and how did that end?

426
00:38:09,360 --> 00:38:10,520
I was the only fool in it.

427
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:12,080
Song...

428
00:38:12,080 --> 00:38:13,200
Don't call me that.

429
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:16,880
If you only called me here to scold me

430
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:18,760
and you won't listen to anything,

431
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:20,320
then I have nothing left to say.

432
00:38:23,080 --> 00:38:24,720
The way you hurt me back then,

433
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:27,000
you've come back and done

434
00:38:27,040 --> 00:38:28,280
the same thing to me again.

435
00:38:28,440 --> 00:38:29,440
Why do you do it?

436
00:38:30,560 --> 00:38:31,800
Why do you keep making me

437
00:38:31,800 --> 00:38:33,000
feel like I have no one left?

438
00:38:45,480 --> 00:38:46,560
I'm sorry.

439
00:39:05,520 --> 00:39:06,560
I'm sorry.

440
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:54,720
(Fee from yesterday included)

441
00:43:05,920 --> 00:43:07,160
What do you take me for,

442
00:43:07,160 --> 00:43:08,440
that you'd treat me like this?

443
00:43:09,280 --> 00:43:10,880
Exactly what you want to be.

444
00:43:12,040 --> 00:43:13,160
Oh,

445
00:43:13,600 --> 00:43:15,240
and last night was good performance.

446
00:43:17,280 --> 00:43:18,880
I thought the two of us could go back

447
00:43:18,880 --> 00:43:19,920
to how we were before.

448
00:43:22,080 --> 00:43:23,880
What do you think you're coming back for,

449
00:43:23,880 --> 00:43:25,360
now that there's nothing left.

450
00:43:40,400 --> 00:43:41,440
What is it, Sarttra?

451
00:43:45,600 --> 00:43:46,720
Okay, I'll come in now.

452
00:44:16,680 --> 00:44:17,680
Hello, Oh?

453
00:44:18,200 --> 00:44:19,440
How's Mom doing, Ong?

454
00:44:20,040 --> 00:44:21,440
She took the new medicine,

455
00:44:21,680 --> 00:44:23,040
so she managed to sleep a bit,

456
00:44:23,360 --> 00:44:24,480
but she still keeps

457
00:44:24,480 --> 00:44:26,160
complaining about aching all over.

458
00:44:27,360 --> 00:44:28,480
Is she eating?

459
00:44:30,720 --> 00:44:31,720
Mm.

460
00:44:32,160 --> 00:44:33,160
A little.

461
00:44:33,800 --> 00:44:34,800
Mm.

462
00:44:35,960 --> 00:44:37,000
Oh,

463
00:44:37,720 --> 00:44:38,840
is something wrong?

464
00:44:39,800 --> 00:44:41,360
Your voice doesn't sound good at all.

465
00:44:43,400 --> 00:44:44,440
Going quiet like that,

466
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:46,160
something's definitely up.

467
00:44:46,800 --> 00:44:47,920
Out with it.

468
00:44:48,320 --> 00:44:50,800
We don't keep secrets from each other.

469
00:44:52,920 --> 00:44:54,240
I've put myself somewhere

470
00:44:54,240 --> 00:44:55,480
I shouldn't be again.

471
00:44:56,880 --> 00:45:00,160
There's only one place you shouldn't be...

472
00:45:03,360 --> 00:45:04,360
That woman?

473
00:45:06,400 --> 00:45:07,360
Mm.

474
00:45:07,440 --> 00:45:08,880
She's my employer.

475
00:45:09,120 --> 00:45:10,640
What? Seriously?

476
00:45:11,880 --> 00:45:14,360
Then why did you take this job?

477
00:45:14,840 --> 00:45:16,920
It took you so long to move on back then.

478
00:45:20,640 --> 00:45:22,680
I only have to endure it for 120 days.

479
00:45:25,080 --> 00:45:26,120
Oh,

480
00:45:27,880 --> 00:45:29,000
honestly,

481
00:45:30,640 --> 00:45:32,080
you still love her, don't you?

482
00:45:35,040 --> 00:45:36,040
Mm.

483
00:45:37,680 --> 00:45:38,800
And does she

484
00:45:39,960 --> 00:45:41,240
know you still love her?

485
00:45:45,360 --> 00:45:47,080
She won't believe anything I say now.

486
00:45:49,320 --> 00:45:50,800
No matter how well I treat her,

487
00:45:51,760 --> 00:45:52,840
she thinks it's fake.

488
00:45:55,280 --> 00:45:57,600
Then just tell her the truth.

489
00:46:01,240 --> 00:46:02,600
It's better to let it end like this.

490
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:06,360
I can't go back

491
00:46:06,360 --> 00:46:07,960
and stand by her side anyway.

492
00:46:09,040 --> 00:46:10,360
We're from different worlds.

493
00:46:14,280 --> 00:46:17,040
Oh, Oh,

494
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:18,760
are you sure you can handle it?

495
00:46:20,520 --> 00:46:21,520
Mm.

496
00:46:21,720 --> 00:46:22,720
Don't worry.

497
00:46:25,920 --> 00:46:27,040
Hug, hug, okay?

498
00:46:30,040 --> 00:46:31,040
Okay, dear.

499
00:47:28,760 --> 00:47:30,600
I heard there's a small diamond show

500
00:47:30,640 --> 00:47:31,720
around here.

501
00:47:32,160 --> 00:47:34,160
I never imagined it would be a RATANA event.

502
00:47:34,240 --> 00:47:35,520
Seat Uncle somewhere good,

503
00:47:36,040 --> 00:47:37,200
so he can see clearly

504
00:47:37,520 --> 00:47:39,360
what's interesting about RATANA's

505
00:47:39,360 --> 00:47:41,040
small diamond show.

506
00:47:41,280 --> 00:47:42,560
Would you mind, Oh,

507
00:47:42,560 --> 00:47:43,640
if I tried to bring back

508
00:47:43,640 --> 00:47:45,080
the old days again?

509
00:47:45,960 --> 00:47:47,920
I guarantee you'll have money to spend and

510
00:47:47,960 --> 00:47:49,160
live in comfort for

511
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:50,720
the rest of your life, Sam.

512
00:47:54,120 --> 00:47:56,520
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

513
00:47:56,520 --> 00:48:00,200
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

514
00:48:00,240 --> 00:48:05,400
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

515
00:48:05,440 --> 00:48:08,600
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

516
00:48:08,640 --> 00:48:13,120
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

517
00:48:13,120 --> 00:48:21,240
♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪

518
00:48:21,240 --> 00:48:27,800
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪
